  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "The solution set of \\(6x^2+5x\\lt4\\) is the set of all values of \\(x\\) such that:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-2\\lt x\\lt1\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\dfrac43\\lt x\\lt\\dfrac12\\)",
    "C": "\\(-\\dfrac12\\lt x\\lt\\dfrac43\\)",
    "D": "\\(x\\lt\\dfrac12\\) or \\(x\\gt-\\dfrac43\\)",
    "E": "\\(x\\lt-\\dfrac43\\) or \\(x\\gt\\dfrac12\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Move everything to the left so that we can determine when a product is negative:\n\\[6x^2+5x-4=(3x+4)(2x-1)<0.\\]\nThe boundary equation \\((3x+4)(2x-1)=0\\) gives \\(x=-\\frac43\\) and \\(x=\\frac12\\).\n\nFor \\(x<-\\frac43\\), both factors are negative, so their product is positive. For \\(-\\frac43<x<\\frac12\\), the first factor is positive and the second is negative, so their product is negative. For \\(x>\\frac12\\), both factors are positive. At either boundary, the product is zero, which does not satisfy the strict inequality.\n\nThus the solution set is \\(\\boxed{-\\frac43<x<\\frac12}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
